------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=900 order templar unknelt
Text=The Knights Templar came out of the siege with their chapter houses standing and their numbers halved. No benefactor ever came for them. You had taken their oath. Then you talked the thing that meant to collect on it into its own death, before it ever reached a chapter house. The order rebuilt slowly, under its own banners and out of its own treasury. For a generation it was poorer than it had been in two hundred years. No record was ever written of what you spared them. The only men who could have written it were standing at Alamut, and they did not understand what they had heard.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=
Custom Action=CTriggerRelayAction
{
Relay Name=Fixt order epilogue relay
}
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=900 order templar relic
Text=You forged the Lion Shield as an initiate. The wish that freed the Crypt was meant to put an old cross on it, with the lion faint beneath. Two hundred years of damned knights had gone free to put it there. No chapter roll records why. When you were gone it went back to the order. They hung it in a hall, and nobody there could say whose it had been.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=
Custom Action=CTriggerRelayAction
{
Relay Name=Fixt order epilogue relay
}
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=900 order templar aegis
Text=You forged the Lion Shield as an initiate, and you carried it out of the Crypt with an old cross on it. Two hundred years of damned knights had gone free to put it there. Sir Roger saw what it was and took it from you, because a relic is a thing the order lays on tombs. He gave you the Aegis, and He gave you the Aegis in its place. The order keeps both now. It tells the story of the second. Nobody there can tell you who the first one was for.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=
Custom Action=CTriggerRelayAction
{
Relay Name=Fixt order epilogue relay
}
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=900 order inquisition exposer
Text=The Inquisition came out of the siege with its command intact, and the city handed it the rebuilding. Part of that standing was your doing. You told them where La Calle Perdida was, and your directions were good, because you had been inside it as a friend. The Holy Office took the quarter apart in nine days. It spent thirty years cataloguing what it found. The men who did the work were promoted on your word. The pyres were lit in the plaza where the markets had been, and the cities paid for the wood.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=
Custom Action=CTriggerRelayAction
{
Relay Name=Fixt order epilogue relay
}
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=900 order inquisition killer
Text=The Inquisition came out of the siege with its command intact, and the city handed it the rebuilding. You had worn its mark and you had killed its own. The Holy Office keeps careful records of a name entered twice. Its fires burned on through the peace as they had through the war, because a frightened city asks its inquisitors for more work, not less. The cities paid for the wood. Nothing was ever charged against you. But there were four towns between Barcelona and Montaillou that you never entered again, and you knew all four names.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=
Custom Action=CTriggerRelayAction
{
Relay Name=Fixt order epilogue relay
}
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=900 order inquisition high
Text=The Inquisition came out of the siege with its command intact, and the city handed it the rebuilding. You had risen high in the Holy Office, high enough that the work reached you as paper. You signed what other men carried out. Its fires burned on through the peace as they had through the war, because a frightened city asks its inquisitors for more work, not less. The cities paid for the wood. Your signature was on enough of it that the archive gave you a box of your own.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
