Node ID=900 order inquisition
Text=The Inquisition came out of the siege with its command intact, and the city handed it the rebuilding. You had worn its mark and done its work. For a few years the mark was worth more than the work had been. It opened doors in the new Barcelona. Then it went on opening doors you no longer wanted to walk through. Its fires burned on through the peace as they had through the war, and the cities paid for the wood. You stopped wearing the mark in the third year. Nobody ever asked you why.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=
Custom Action=CTriggerRelayAction
{
Relay Name=Fixt order epilogue relay
}
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=900 order cult ended
Text=The Dark Inquisitors did not survive you. You found them on the northern plains and you ended what they were doing there. Their habits were burned where they lay. The shepherds brought their flocks back within the year. Nobody in Barcelona asked what had happened, because nobody in Barcelona wanted the answer. The Holy Office went on saying that such men had never been its own. You knew better. You had seen the habits.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=
Custom Action=CTriggerRelayAction
{
Relay Name=Fixt order epilogue relay
}
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=900 order cult told
Text=The Dark Inquisitors did not survive you. You found them on the northern plains, you ended them, and you told Torquemada to his face. He paid you and he kept his word. It was never written down. The Holy Office holds no record of the cult, or the habits, or the men who wore them. Within a generation you were the last who knew. He had called it rot from inside the house. The house stayed standing, and nobody ever looked for the rest.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=
Custom Action=CTriggerRelayAction
{
Relay Name=Fixt order epilogue relay
}
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=900 order cult ended dead
Text=You ended the Dark Inquisitors on the plains, and you ended Torquemada in his own chambers. The Holy Office lost its heretics and its head to the same hand. It could not praise you for the first without naming you for the second. So it did neither. Both entries were struck from the record. In the archive, the two pages sit side by side with nothing written on them.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=
Custom Action=CTriggerRelayAction
{
Relay Name=Fixt order epilogue relay
}
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=900 order cult served
Text=The Dark Inquisitors paid what they promised. Bishop Diego was dead on the south road, and nobody was left to write letters about them. They grew. Their habits spread from the northern plains to the hill towns, and then to parishes that had never heard the name. Within ten years it was hard to say where the cult stopped and the Holy Office began. Some of them knew your name. They said it the way the faithful say a saint's.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=
Custom Action=CTriggerRelayAction
{
Relay Name=Fixt order epilogue relay
}
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=900 order cult inherited
Text=The Dark Inquisitors paid you for Bishop Diego. Nobody paid you for Torquemada, and they never had to. The Holy Office was still fighting over his chair when they came down from the plains, in good habits, with good letters. There was no honest bishop left to read them. Within a generation the chair was theirs, and few could have said when it changed. The fires had burned low. They burned again, and no city was asked to pay for the wood.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=
Custom Action=CTriggerRelayAction
{
Relay Name=Fixt order epilogue relay
}
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=900 order saladin killer
Text=The Knights of Saladin kept the pact of east and west after the west had stopped keeping it. After Alamut they kept it alone. You had been a guest in their tents in the Gate District and you had killed one of their knights. The order wrote down both without comment, which is their way of closing a matter. They held the eastern shrines for two generations against raids the west never heard about. They were called weak for it by men who had never fought them. Guests at their table were told your name, and told it carefully, as part of a longer lesson about hospitality.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=
Custom Action=CTriggerRelayAction
{
Relay Name=Fixt order epilogue relay
}
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=900 order saladin high
Text=The Knights of Saladin kept the pact of east and west after the west had stopped keeping it. After Alamut they kept it alone. You had been named a Favored One, the first westerner in living memory given the title. They held the eastern shrines for two generations against raids the west never heard about. They were called weak for it by men who had never fought them. Your name stayed in the recitation at Alamut long after anybody there could have said what you looked like.
Should Have Voiceover=1

