Text=The Inquisition entered the siege without a head, and without the man who would have been the next one. You owed the Holy Office nothing, and you killed them both. Nobody was left to write a fever. Its would-be successors fought over the chair for years. The fires did not go out, but they burned low. Within ten years, some cities stopped paying for the wood. No one in those cities knew your name. The Holy Office did. It never again had the strength to do anything about it.
