Node ID=900 order wielder ring
Text=La Calle Perdida was never found, because by the end of that year there was nothing left of it to find. You put on Relican's ring and turned it on the hidden city yourself. The few who walked out gave you the only title that fit: Dark Lord of a place that no longer existed. What the Church had spent a century failing to drown, you buried in an afternoon. Whatever books it still held went down with it. Nobody tapped the Ways crystals for it again. Nobody taught any of it in the open, then or afterward.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=
Custom Action=CTriggerRelayAction
{
Relay Name=Fixt order epilogue relay
}
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=900 order wielder exposed
Text=La Calle Perdida was found, and it was found because you told the Inquisition where to look. You had been inside as a friend first, which is the only reason your directions were good enough. The Holy Office took the quarter apart in nine days. What the Wielders had kept hidden for a century was catalogued, carted out and burned in the open. Cedric's own house went in the third load. A handful got away through the sewers. They taught what they could remember to people who did not understand what they were being given, and inside two generations it was gone.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=
Custom Action=CTriggerRelayAction
{
Relay Name=Fixt order epilogue relay
}
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=900 order wielder killer
Text=La Calle Perdida was never found, not by the Inquisition and not by the knights. You had walked its streets as a friend and left Wielder dead behind you. In a city that small, both were known before you reached the gate. The magic the Church had tried to drown went on under the streets without you. It was taught in the open again long after everyone who had hidden it was dead. The door you had been given was not opened a second time. They never hunted you for it, which was its own kind of answer.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=
Custom Action=CTriggerRelayAction
{
Relay Name=Fixt order epilogue relay
}
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=900 order wielder high
Text=La Calle Perdida was never found, not by the Inquisition and not by the knights. After the siege it took in more of Barcelona's unwanted than it had room for. You had risen high among the Wielders, a scion of Richard's line who chose the sorcerers over the cross. That choice was argued over in both houses for a century. The magic the Church had tried to drown went on breathing under the streets. It was taught in the open again long after everyone who had hidden it was dead. When it was, the first teachers cited you, and got the details wrong.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=
Custom Action=CTriggerRelayAction
