Node ID=900 order horde traitor
Text=The goblin tribes came down out of the mountains, counted themselves, and discovered that they had two claimants and one rock. You handed the Khan's east rock to Butu's heir, and you were paid for it. The Horde has a word for that, and the word is not Champion. What might have been a war against the border towns was a war inside Khara'Khorum instead. It ran three generations and ended with fewer goblins than it started with. They remembered you accurately, which was the worst of it. Of all the names that came out of that war, yours was the one they taught to children.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=
Custom Action=CTriggerRelayAction
{
Relay Name=Fixt order epilogue relay
}
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=900 order horde high
Text=The goblin tribes came down out of the mountains, counted themselves, and found that they were many. Nothing in the west was counting at all. You had been their Champion, and when the banner went up your name was stitched beside the Khan's on it, in a script you could not read. A Khan's banner rose again inside three generations. The border towns burned first, then the valley forts. The chronicles of the west recorded the whole thing as a surprise. In Khara'Khorum it had been expected for ninety years, and they were still telling the story with your name in it.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=
