------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=900 order savage heart
Text=The Savage Heart came out of the war the way mercenary companies do, which is richer and with a shorter roster. You took Raylark's contract and signed on to hunt goblins for the bounty, counted by the scalp. The company's books still carry the entry under your name. In the years after Alamut half of Europe wanted men who would do that sort of work and not ask after the paperwork. The Savage Heart raised its rate twice in five years. Raylark kept his camp west of Khara'Khorum until he was too old to hold it. The Horde had learned to count western killers by name, and yours was one of the names.
