Node ID=900 friend cortes no verdict
Text=You declined to settle it. Shylocke said he would take the matter to the magistrates, and he did. They had no patience for either man and split the difference badly. Cortes kept half a ship and a debt he could not service. "I suppose I should not have rested my hopes on a stranger," he had said. Shylocke billed him for the magistrates' time as well, and collected.
Should Have Voiceover=1

